// How the Runner links pb_mapper_ffi, the app's Rust core, built as a static
// library by scripts/build/pb-mapper-ffi-ios.sh. Nothing the linker sees
// refers to it: Dart reaches it through DynamicLibrary.process() and the
// desktop video plugin (ui/darwin/DesktopVideo.swift) through dlsym, so a
// plain -l would take none of it.
// - -force_load links every member of the library.
// - -export_dynamic keeps its global entry points (pb_mapper_*) exported, and
//   alive should dead stripping be turned on.
// - STRIP_STYLE = non-global keeps them through an archive's strip.
// - A static library does not carry its system dependencies. These are the
//   frameworks and libraries its crates link for aarch64-apple-ios
//   (#[link] attributes and build scripts of core-foundation-sys, objc2,
//   netdev, objc2-security, system-configuration and libc); libSystem comes
//   by default.
OTHER_LDFLAGS = $(inherited) -force_load "$(PROJECT_DIR)/../native/ios/libpb_mapper_ffi.a" -Wl,-export_dynamic -framework CoreFoundation -framework Foundation -framework Network -framework Security -framework SystemConfiguration -lobjc -liconv
STRIP_STYLE = non-global
